From dd5cca9f7cf295cfabace6879652fd08adc9e4bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RINNECODER <93304526+RINNECODER@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:05:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Prompt-lookup drafts for Flint (streamed too): rewind its
 sliding-window rings

A rejected draft's keys stayed in a BatchRotatingKVCache past trim(): the next
one-token step trims the ring from its length, not its _idx, so they stayed in
the window. _solo_rewind now cuts them off; a multi-token pass leaves the ring
in order and window-1 + T long, so nothing the kept tokens need is lost.
The solo path also recognises flint_streamed (RecursiveSI/flint-int4), which
it missed by module name. LOCALS_DRAFTS=0 turns drafts off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
